1 focus:outline-none\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"CreativeWork\",\"@id\":\"https://mehrdad.ir/work/kilika-fintech#project\",\"name\":\"kilika\",\"alternateName\":\"کلیکا\",\"description\":\"A banking-focused fintech super-app: software for modern financial services. Now at MVP stage — the full pitch deck is published on this site.\",\"url\":\"https://mehrdad.ir/work/kilika-fintech\",\"creator\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"@id\":\"https://mehrdad.ir/#person\",\"name\":\"Mehrdad\",\"url\":\"https://mehrdad.ir/\"}}</script><article class=\"mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6\"><div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3\"><span data-slot=\"badge\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium w-fit whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 [&amp;&gt;svg]:size-3 gap-1 [&amp;&gt;svg]:pointer-events-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive transition-[color,box-shadow] overflow-hidden border-transparent [a&amp;]:hover:bg-secondary/90 bg-fuchsia-600/10 text-fuchsia-700 dark:text-fuchsia-400\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-presentation me-1 h-3 w-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M2 3h20\"></path><path d=\"M21 3v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V3\"></path><path d=\"m7 21 5-5 5 5\"></path></svg>MVP</span><span class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400\">0%</span></div><h1 class=\"mt-4 text-3xl font-extrabold leading-tight sm:text-4xl\">kilika</h1><div class=\"prose-blog mt-8\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A banking-focused fintech super-app: software for modern financial services. Now at MVP stage — the full pitch deck is published on this site.</p></div><div class=\"mt-6\"><div class=\"rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-gradient-to-br from-amber-500/10 to-orange-500/10 p-5\"><p class=\"text-sm leading-relaxed\" dir=\"ltr\">The full pitch deck of this product is live:</p><div class=\"mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3\"><a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/s/kilika.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-flex h-11 items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-xl border border-amber-500/40 bg-background/70 px-5 text-sm font-bold text-amber-700 shadow-sm transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-amber-500 hover:shadow-md focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-amber-500 focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-background dark:text-amber-300\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-presentation h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M2 3h20\"></path><path d=\"M21 3v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V3\"></path><path d=\"m7 21 5-5 5 5\"></path></svg>Pitch deck<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-external-link h-4 w-4 opacity-80\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M15 3h6v6\"></path><path d=\"M10 14 21 3\"></path><path d=\"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6\"></path></svg></a></div></div></div><div class=\"prose-blog mt-10\" dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote><p>kilika is a super-app and middleware platform — one platform for access to dozens of online services; a simple, unified experience for transport, shopping, travel and everyday services.</p></blockquote><h2>The Problem We Solve</h2><p><strong>The digital world is fragmented.</strong> In an era where technology should simplify life, users are still drowning in unnecessary complexity:</p><ul><li><strong>Time wasted switching between apps:</strong> users switch between different apps 20+ times a day — at least 15 minutes of lost time daily.</li><li><strong>No intelligence in online services:</strong> every service operates in isolation; no smart connection exists between a user's different needs.</li><li><strong>Inconsistent, complex user experience:</strong> learning and using 8+ different interfaces creates a genuinely complicated process.</li></ul><p><strong>Hidden costs for users:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Different fees</strong> — every platform charges its own commission.</li><li><strong>Price opacity</strong> — comparing prices across services is difficult.</li><li><strong>Scattered discounts</strong> — loyalty points live separately inside each app.</li><li><strong>Fragmented payment methods</strong> — a card must be added to every service.</li></ul><p><strong>Business-side pains:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>High customer-acquisition cost</strong> — every platform spends on its own marketing.</li><li><strong>High churn</strong> — users drift between apps.</li><li><strong>No cross-selling</strong> — complementary services cannot be offered.</li><li><strong>Siloed data</strong> — behavior analysis is capped at one service.</li></ul><h2>The Ecosystem Gap</h2><p>Leading global markets have already moved to integration:</p><ul><li><strong>WeChat — China:</strong> 1.3+ billion active users; payments, social, shopping, transport.</li><li><strong>Paytm — India:</strong> 450 million users; digital wallet, banking, insurance.</li><li><strong>Gojek — Indonesia:</strong> 190 million users; transport, food, payments, logistics.</li></ul><p><strong>Iran — with 85 million internet users — still has no national super-app.</strong> This is a unique opportunity to create multi-billion-dollar economic value.</p><h2>The Solution: One App; Every Service</h2><p>kilika is an intelligent platform that puts dozens of online services behind one simple, secure app:</p><ul><li><strong>One app; every service</strong> — all everyday services behind a single entry point.</li><li><strong>Speed and simplicity</strong> — no more installing multiple apps and constant switching.</li><li><strong>Unified security</strong> — authenticate once; access every service securely.</li></ul><p><strong>Product strategy: an Iranian and an international version.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Iranian version (Phase 1):</strong> local services (Snapp; Digikala; Alibaba.ir); integration with Iranian banks; full Persian-language support; compliance with domestic regulations; launch in the Iranian market.</li><li><strong>International version (Phase 2):</strong> global services (Uber; Amazon; Booking); international-currency support; multilingual (English; Arabic; Turkish and more); global standards compliance; expansion into the Middle East and Central Asia.</li></ul><p>How it works is simple: the user installs kilika; gets access to every service; kilika connects to the partner services.</p><h2>Market Opportunity</h2><p>The global super-app market is moving at extraordinary speed:</p><ul><li><strong>Global digital-wallet market:</strong> $11.4B (2026) — projected $27.3B (2031); 19.1% CAGR.</li><li><strong>Iran:</strong> 850 trillion toman in annual digital transactions (1404); 45 million active mobile-internet users; 75% growth in online transactions year over year; 12M+ monthly active users across partner platforms; 65% preference for a unified wallet (survey-based).</li></ul><h2>Platform Capabilities</h2><ul><li><strong>Unified account management</strong> — centralized balance and transaction management with top-ups from every bank.</li><li><strong>One-click payment</strong> — instant transactions without re-entering card details.</li><li><strong>Service connections</strong> — integration with Snapp; Tapsi; Digikala; exchanges; stores; mobile operators.</li><li><strong>Multi-layer security</strong> — banking-grade encryption; two-factor authentication; fraud monitoring.</li><li><strong>Smart analytics</strong> — precise spending reports and automatic transaction categorization.</li><li><strong>Excellent UX</strong> — a simple, fast interface across every device.</li></ul><h2>Revenue Model: Four Independent Streams</h2><ul><li><strong>Transaction commission — 55%:</strong> 0.5–2% of every purchase/payment transaction (Digikala purchases; Snapp payments; mobile top-ups). Detail: goods & services 1.5–2% (40% of volume); transport 1–1.5% (30%); top-ups & bills 0.5–1% (20%); digital services the remaining 10% of volume.</li><li><strong>Store partnerships — 25%:</strong> B2B contracts and sales commissions — monthly subscriptions from 50M toman; 1–3% sales commission; ad campaigns 10–50M toman; data/analytics reports 2–10M toman. Deck example: a 100-branch retail chain pays 20M toman/month subscription + 2% sales commission = 50–100M toman monthly revenue.</li><li><strong>Financial services — 15%:</strong> float income and currency/gold conversion and short-term credit and transaction insurance. With an average 100B toman balance on the platform; 3B toman annual income (3%) from bank deposits.</li><li><strong>Premium services — 5%:</strong> personal VIP account 20K toman/month (50% lower commission; instant withdrawals; 24/7 support); Business account 100–500K toman/month (multi-account management; dedicated API; automated invoicing); Enterprise API 5–20M toman/month.</li></ul><p><strong>Monthly revenue with 1M users: 18B toman</strong> — transaction commission 9.9B + store partnerships 4.5B + financial services 2.7B + premium 0.9B.</p><p><strong>Key metrics:</strong> average transaction value 250K toman; average commission per transaction 1,500 toman; 12 transactions per user per month; monthly revenue per user 18K toman; customer-acquisition cost (CAC) 150K toman; payback 8.3 months.</p><p><strong>Why it is sustainable:</strong> four independent revenue streams (lower dependency risk) + recurring, predictable income + a net profit margin above 65%.</p><h2>B2B Partnerships and the Developer API</h2><p>Why should established apps like Snapp; Tapsi and Digikala use kilika's services?</p><ul><li><strong>User satisfaction +35%</strong> — unified services and a better experience.</li><li><strong>Support costs −40%</strong> — a sharp drop in support calls and tickets.</li><li><strong>Support-team load −50%</strong> — fewer technical issues and repetitive questions.</li><li><strong>App usefulness +60%</strong> — turning an app into a full super-app.</li><li><strong>Developer API up to 90% faster</strong> — integration in under a week instead of months (payments; top-ups & bills; reporting; encryption; authentication; monitoring; a behavioral-analytics dashboard with forecasting).</li><li><strong>Partner revenue +45%</strong> — users use the app more = more revenue.</li></ul><p>Deck conclusion: partner apps — with +35% satisfaction and −40% support costs — reach positive ROI in the first month of cooperation.</p><h2>Competitive Position</h2><p><strong>kilika vs Blubank:</strong> Blubank offers limited banking services — payments-only focus; no integration with everyday services; a traditional digital-banking approach. kilika offers 20+ integrated service categories (banking + shopping + transport + travel) — 20× more capabilities; a powerful developer API; a next-generation super-app; and an international version: launching in Persian-Gulf countries in year one — a financial bridge between Iran and the world.</p><p><strong>kilika vs App:</strong> App is capped at payments and money transfer — years without notable innovation; an outdated, complicated UI; weak phone-call-only support. kilika is an innovative next-gen super-app — a modern interface; smart 24/7 support (chat; voice; video); payments + banking + shopping + transport + travel in one place; connections to every major national platform; a complete developer ecosystem (SDK & API). User journey: ~10 minutes in App with switching between several apps; ~1 minute in kilika — everything in one place.</p><p><strong>Migration potential:</strong> a projected 30–50% of App users moving in year one; a 10× value proposition at a 70% lower acquisition cost; super-apps command 3–5× the valuation of single-purpose apps; 100+ integrated features from day one; 80% of budget on marketing; 2–3× user lifetime value (LTV).</p><h2>Next-Gen Neobanks and the Digital Movement</h2><p>kilika has three layers: a <strong>next-generation neobank</strong> (complete digital banking + advanced financial services + everyday-life integration — beyond Blubank and Digipay); a <strong>true middleware</strong> (connections to every service and platform without leaving the kilika environment); a <strong>smart super-app</strong> (AI + personalized suggestions + a unified experience). With 80% of the budget allocated to marketing, kilika is not just an app but a digital movement that will set a new standard for neobanks and middleware super-apps in the region — the primary ad target is Generations Z & Y; market leadership within two years. The innovations are legally protected too: patents (novel algorithms and technologies); trademarks (brand and visual identity); NDA contracts with partners; software rights (source code and system architecture).</p><h2>The 1-Million-User Year-One Guarantee</h2><p>Access to 15M+ potential users through 11 B2B customer categories:</p><ul><li><strong>Transport (high priority):</strong> Snapp 8M; Tapsi 6M; Maxim 2M users.</li><li><strong>Online retail:</strong> Digikala 15M; Digipay 5M; Azki 3M.</li><li><strong>Chain stores:</strong> Ofogh Koorosh 3M; Shahrvand 2M; Daily Market 1.5M; Refah 1.8M.</li><li><strong>Mobile operators:</strong> MCI 55M; Irancell 48M; Rightel 12M subscribers.</li><li><strong>Other categories:</strong> travel & ticketing (Alibaba 12M; SnappTrip 4M); cafés & restaurants; professional services; offline retail (10M local stores); banking & finance; social networks; government & public sector.</li></ul><p>125K+ potential customers in active pursuit; 144M annual transactions with 1M users. <strong>Network effect: one customer; every customer.</strong> Landing one big customer (say Snapp or Digikala) forces the competitors and complements to join too, just to stay competitive: land one big platform → rivals need kilika → exponential network growth.</p><h2>The Bank-Partner Advantage</h2><ul><li><strong>Payment-gateway transactions +50% to +200%</strong> in the first two years — with full service integration, every transport/shopping/travel/services payment runs through the partner bank's gateway.</li><li><strong>Banking transactions +10% to +100%</strong> — new users; more daily transactions; a dynamic financial ecosystem.</li></ul><p>The goal: turning the partner bank into the digital-payments market leader — with access to the country's largest online-transaction ecosystem.</p><h2>For Investors</h2><p>Requested funding: <strong>$4M</strong>; official presentation February 2026. Projection: given the revenue diversity (commissions; advertising; subscriptions; API) and the large user base, kilika's revenue surpasses Blubank's within the first three years — a multi-layer business model; fast cash flow; a higher valuation. This text is the deck itself, written out in full; <a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/s/kilika.html\">the original kilika pitch-deck page</a> is live on the site's main domain.</p></div><div class=\"mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-gradient-to-br from-amber-500/10 to-orange-500/10 p-5 sm:p-6\"><div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3\"><a href=\"https://kilika-app.vercel.app/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-flex h-12 items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-500 to-orange-500 px-6 font-bold text-white shadow-lg shadow-amber-500/25 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0